WEBVTT

00:58:27.196 --> 00:58:31.466
CA: Your book and your talk
have framed AI as this --

00:58:31.490 --> 00:58:33.125
There are really two main players,

00:58:33.149 --> 00:58:37.672
that US and China are holding
most of the cards right now.

00:58:37.696 --> 00:58:41.029
That leaves five billion
people in the world

00:58:41.053 --> 00:58:42.910
who aren't in those countries.

00:58:42.934 --> 00:58:44.355
What would you say to them --

00:58:44.379 --> 00:58:46.536
how worried should they be
about their future,

00:58:46.560 --> 00:58:50.983
is there something that their governments
should do to mitigate the fact

00:58:51.007 --> 00:58:53.085
that they're not currently an AI leader?

00:58:53.656 --> 00:58:56.831
KFL: I think the inequality
among countries

00:58:56.855 --> 00:59:01.760
is as big a problem
as the inequality within countries.